-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 40: CORRUPTION, DRUG TRAFFICKING AND OTHER SERIOUS CRIMES (CONFISCATION OF BENEFITS) ACT (part roc9, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- How to read a result: see the header of roc9-order-41.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING; never turn NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- THE SHAPES THIS ORDER REPEATS.
-- * "must be filed and served ... on A, B and C at least 7 clear days before the hearing": one record per rule of how each person
--   stands (served / not served / there is no such person), a Period constant, and one function.  The period is checked against the
--   last day that Order 3, Rule 3 computes (an input); a late filing or service is JUST FALSE (a period the text fixes in its own
--   words); a person not yet served is NOTHING (a bare "must", QB).  Filing comes from Order 28, Rule 10 and service from Order 7,
--   Rule 8 (both inputs): the day of the last service is the day asked.
-- * "the supporting affidavit must state (a) ... (b) ...": one record per rule of what it states, and one function that is
--   JUST TRUE when each required statement is made, NOTHING otherwise (QB).  A statement required only "where" or "as the case may
--   be" has three states (stated / not stated / not applicable on these facts).
-- * The Court's directions ("Unless the Court otherwise directs") are the text's own exception and are asked where the text says so.

§ `Order 40 -- Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act`

