GIVEN `the statute is the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 1(1) a statute is the Act` MEANS
    IF `the statute is the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Act” means the Corruption, Drug Trafficking and Other Serious Crimes (Confiscation of Benefits) Act"

-- The deeming of a reference to a section is lifted by the text's own exception, so the exception makes the requirement not apply.
