-- How a person to be served stands (used by every service rule of this Order).  "there is no such person" is for a person
-- the text asks about only where there is one ("any person having any interest", "the receiver, where one has been appointed").
DECLARE `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` IS ONE OF
    `o 40 r 2(4) served`
    `o 40 r 2(4) not served`
    `o 40 r 2(4) there is no such person`

-- FORK QB | bare "must be served": the person is not served | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the person does not exist: this function answers NOTHING and `o 40 r 2(4) the duty to serve the person arises` answers JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE ("nothing is unmet")
