`o 40 r 2(4) the person to be served has been served` MEANS
    CONSIDER status
    WHEN `o 40 r 2(4) served` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 40 r 2(4) not served` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); the Rule does not say what follows
    WHEN `o 40 r 2(4) there is no such person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise (QD); the companion function answers JUST FALSE

