    IF     `the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit`
       AND contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(a) the grounds for believing that the defendant has derived benefits from drug dealing or criminal conduct, as the case may be`
       AND (contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(i) that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars) and that they have not been concluded` EQUALS `o 40 r 2(1) it is stated` OR contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(i) that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars) and that they have not been concluded` EQUALS `o 40 r 2(1) it is not applicable on these facts`)
       AND (contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(ii) that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence` EQUALS `o 40 r 2(1) it is stated` OR contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(ii) that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence` EQUALS `o 40 r 2(1) it is not applicable on these facts`)
       AND (contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(iii) that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction` EQUALS `o 40 r 2(1) it is stated` OR contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(iii) that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction` EQUALS `o 40 r 2(1) it is not applicable on these facts`)
       AND contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(c) full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, specifying the person or persons holding such property, as far as the deponent is able to provide`
       AND (`proceedings have been instituted against the defendant` OR contents's `o 40 r 5(1)(d) an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 40 r 5(1) does not say what follows when something required is missing


