    PARTY `o 40 r 6(3) the Public Prosecutor`
    MUST `o 40 r 6(3)(a) serve copies of the restraint order and the supporting affidavit`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `o 40 r 6(3) the Public Prosecutor`
        MUST `o 40 r 6(3)(b) notify all other persons or bodies affected by the restraint order of its terms`
    )

-- src:5660 | (4) Where a charging order is made, the Public Prosecutor must — ( a )
-- src:5661 | unless the Court otherwise directs, serve copies of the order and supporting affidavit on the defendant and, where property to which the order relates is held by another person, on that person; and
-- src:5662 | ( b )
-- src:5663 | serve a copy of the order on the Accountant ‑ General or a company, as is appropriate.
@ref O 40 r 6(4) (src:5660-5663)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 40 r 6(3) party` `o 40 r 6(3) action`
`o 40 r 6(4) the duties of the Public Prosecutor on a charging order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 40 r 6(3) the Public Prosecutor`
    MUST `o 40 r 6(4)(a) serve copies of the charging order and the supporting affidavit`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `o 40 r 6(3) the Public Prosecutor`
        MUST `o 40 r 6(4)(b) serve a copy of the charging order on the Accountant-General or a company`
    )

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 40 Rule 7 -- discharge or variation of an order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 7(1): "Any person or body on whom a restraint order or a charging order is served or who is notified of such an order
-- may apply to discharge or vary the order."  A scope limit with no "only".
-- src:5665 | 7. —(1) Any person or body on whom a restraint order or a charging order is served or who is notified of such an order may apply to discharge or vary the order. (2) The summons and any supporting affidavit must be filed and served on — ( a )
@ref O 40 r 7(1) (src:5665)
GIVEN `a restraint order or a charging order is served on the person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or body is notified of such an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 7(1) the person or body may apply to discharge or vary the order` MEANS
    IF `a restraint order or a charging order is served on the person or body` OR `the person or body is notified of such an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person or body on whom a restraint order or a charging order is served or who is notified of such an order"

-- src:5665 | 7. —(1) Any person or body on whom a restraint order or a charging order is served or who is notified of such an order may apply to discharge or vary the order. (2) The summons and any supporting affidavit must be filed and served on — ( a )
-- src:5666 | the Public Prosecutor; and
-- src:5667 | ( b )
-- src:5668 | the defendant where the defendant is not the applicant,
-- src:5669 | at least 2 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application.
@ref O 40 r 7(2) (src:5665-5669)
`o 40 r 7(2) the period before the hearing` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 2
    `period unit` IS `Clear days`
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

DECLARE `o 40 r 7(2) the persons to be served` HAS
    `o 40 r 7(2)(a) service on the Public Prosecutor` IS A `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person`
    `o 40 r 7(2)(b) service on the defendant where the defendant is not the applicant` IS A `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person`

-- FORK QB | bare "must" (at least 2 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application): a required person is not yet served, or the document is not filed | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | a person who does not exist ("where" or "any person" unmet) is not served: the per-person function answers NOTHING and `o 40 r 2(4) the duty to serve the person arises` answers JUST FALSE; here such a person counts as met | the whole function answering NOTHING
-- src:5665 | 7. —(1) Any person or body on whom a restraint order or a charging order is served or who is notified of such an order may apply to discharge or vary the order. (2) The summons and any supporting affidavit must be filed and served on — ( a )
-- src:5666 | the Public Prosecutor; and
-- src:5667 | ( b )
-- src:5668 | the defendant where the defendant is not the applicant,
-- src:5669 | at least 2 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application.
@ref O 40 r 7(2) (src:5665-5669)
GIVEN `the summons and any supporting affidavit are filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed` IS A Moment
      `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      persons IS A `o 40 r 7(2) the persons to be served`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 7(2) the summons and any supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the summons and any supporting affidavit are filed` AND `o 40 r 2(4) the person to be served has been served` (persons's `o 40 r 7(2)(a) service on the Public Prosecutor`) EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`o 40 r 2(4) the duty to serve the person arises` (persons's `o 40 r 7(2)(b) service on the defendant where the defendant is not the applicant`) EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `o 40 r 2(4) the person to be served has been served` (persons's `o 40 r 7(2)(b) service on the defendant where the defendant is not the applicant`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 40 r 7(2) does not say what follows when the document is not filed or a required person is not served
           IF (`o 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed`'s `day of the moment`) GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` OR `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least 2 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


