-- FORK F40.1 | "by the Public Prosecutor or, where the case is one of urgency, by way of an application without notice": the urgency limb names a manner of applying (without notice), so the applicant stays the Public Prosecutor and the function does not take the applicant as an input | the urgency limb opens the application to persons other than the Public Prosecutor
-- Rule 8(1): "Where a restraint order or a charging order has been made, an application may be made by the Public Prosecutor
-- or, where the case is one of urgency, by way of an application without notice (a) to discharge or vary such order; (b) for a
-- restraint order or a charging order in respect of other realisable property; or (c) for the appointment of a receiver."
