@ref O 40 r 10(2) (src:5691-5692)
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 10(2) an affidavit of fitness or security is necessary` MEANS
    IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Court otherwise orders" -- the exception lifts the flat negative and the paragraph then says nothing (QA)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not necessary for an affidavit of fitness to be sworn or for the Public Trustee to give security"

-- The same paragraph as the question a party asks, "is the exemption still in force?": JUST TRUE until the Court otherwise orders, JUST FALSE once it has.
-- src:5691 | 10. —(1) Subject to this Rule, Order 13, Rule 9 applies where the Public Trustee is appointed as receiver pursuant to a charging order or under section 16 or 19. (2) It is not necessary for an affidavit of fitness to be sworn or for the Public Trustee to give security, unless the Court otherwise orders.
-- src:5692 | (3) Where the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order and any sums remain in the hands of the Public Trustee, the Public Trustee must apply for directions as to the distribution of such sums.
@ref O 40 r 10(2) (src:5691-5692)
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 10(2) the exemption from an affidavit of fitness and security applies` MEANS
    IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders" -- the exemption ends when the Court orders otherwise
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Rule 10(3): "Where the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order and any sums remain in the
-- hands of the Public Trustee, the Public Trustee must apply for directions as to the distribution of such sums."
-- src:5692 | (3) Where the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order and any sums remain in the hands of the Public Trustee, the Public Trustee must apply for directions as to the distribution of such sums.
-- src:5693 | (4) The application must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit on — ( a )
@ref O 40 r 10(3) (src:5692-5693)
GIVEN `the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sums remain in the hands of the Public Trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 10(3) the Public Trustee's duty to apply for directions arises` MEANS
    IF `the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order` AND `sums remain in the hands of the Public Trustee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order and any sums remain in the hands of the Public Trustee"

-- src:5692 | (3) Where the Public Trustee has fully paid the amount payable under the confiscation order and any sums remain in the hands of the Public Trustee, the Public Trustee must apply for directions as to the distribution of such sums.
-- src:5693 | (4) The application must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit on — ( a )
@ref O 40 r 10(3) (src:5692-5693)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 40 r 6(3) party` `o 40 r 6(3) action`
`o 40 r 10(3) the duty of the Public Trustee to apply for directions` MEANS
    PARTY `o 40 r 10(3) the Public Trustee`
    MUST `o 40 r 10(3) apply for directions as to the distribution of the sums remaining`

-- src:5693 | (4) The application must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit on — ( a )
-- src:5694 | the defendant; and
-- src:5695 | ( b )
-- src:5696 | any other person who held property realised by the receiver,
-- src:5697 | at least 7 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application.
@ref O 40 r 10(4) (src:5693-5697)
`o 40 r 10(4) the period before the hearing` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 7
    `period unit` IS `Clear days`
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

DECLARE `o 40 r 10(4) the persons to be served` HAS
    `o 40 r 10(4)(a) service on the defendant` IS A `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person`
    `o 40 r 10(4)(b) service on any other person who held property realised by the receiver` IS A `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person`

-- FORK QB | bare "must" (at least 7 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application): a required person is not yet served, or the document is not filed | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | a person who does not exist ("where" or "any person" unmet) is not served: the per-person function answers NOTHING and `o 40 r 2(4) the duty to serve the person arises` answers JUST FALSE; here such a person counts as met | the whole function answering NOTHING
-- src:5693 | (4) The application must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit on — ( a )
-- src:5694 | the defendant; and
-- src:5695 | ( b )
-- src:5696 | any other person who held property realised by the receiver,
-- src:5697 | at least 7 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application.
@ref O 40 r 10(4) (src:5693-5697)
GIVEN `the application and the supporting affidavit are filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed` IS A Moment
      `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      persons IS A `o 40 r 10(4) the persons to be served`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 40 r 10(4) the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the application and the supporting affidavit are filed` AND `o 40 r 2(4) the person to be served has been served` (persons's `o 40 r 10(4)(a) service on the defendant`) EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`o 40 r 2(4) the duty to serve the person arises` (persons's `o 40 r 10(4)(b) service on any other person who held property realised by the receiver`) EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `o 40 r 2(4) the person to be served has been served` (persons's `o 40 r 10(4)(b) service on any other person who held property realised by the receiver`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 40 r 10(4) does not say what follows when the document is not filed or a required person is not served
           IF (`o 28 r 10 the moment the document is deemed filed`'s `day of the moment`) GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` OR `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least 7 clear days before the date fixed for the hearing of the application"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


